Protein name: KRT10-binding region domain of the pneumococcal serine
Organism: Streptococcus pneumoniae TIGR4
PDB ID: 3ZGH
Experimental method (X-ray, Cryo-EM, NMR, etc.): X-ray diffraction
Resolution (if available): 2.0 Å
Biological significance: The KRT10-binding domain of the pneumococcal serine-rich repeat protein (PsrP) functions as a lung-specific adhesion and virulence factor.
